\section{Theory} 

\subsection{8-staged symmetric block cipher pipeline}

An eight staged symmetric block cipher crypto pipeline to improve advanced encryption standard based on meta DES, 3DES with P-Box S-Box.

The following image shows you an example of a symmetric cipher 8 staged encryption pipe and the corresponding decryption inverse pipe.

\begin{figure}
\includegraphics[width=1\textwidth,natwidth=868,natheight=402]{CipherPipeline.eps}
\caption{\label{fig:CipherPipeline.eps}Cipher Pipeline}
\end{figure}

Before entering the encryption pipe, the file can be zipped to avoid huge amount of symmetric cipher blocks and after exiting the encryption pipe the file can be ascii encoded with base64 mime, uuencode, xxencode or hex16, because symmetric chiphered binary files might lose their block padding.

Implementation is based on my blog article: \href{https://area23-at.blogspot.com/2024/04/making-symetric-chiffer-encryption.html}{Making symmetric cipher encryption meta permutating again}, including the follwing symmetric cipher algorithms:

\dots or bullet points \dots
\begin{itemize}
\item \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advanced_Encryption_Standard}{Aes}, AesLight, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advanced_Encryption_Standard}{Rijndael}
\item \href{https://www.schneier.com/}{Bruce Schneier's} BlowFish, 2-Fish, 3-Fish
\item \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camellia_(cipher)}{Camellia}, CamelliaLight
\item \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CAST-128}{Cast5}, Cast6
\item \href{https://nsa.gov/}{National security agency's} Des, 3-Des, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skipjack_(cipher)}{SkipJack}
\item \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kupyna}{Dstu7624}
\item \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GOST_(block_cipher)}{Ghost}, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Data_Encryption_Algorithm}{Idea}, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NOEKEON}{Noekeon}
\item \href{https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/RC2_(Blockchiffre)}{RC2}, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RC5}{RC5}32, RC564, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RC6}{RC6}
\item \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SEED}{SEED}, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SM4_(cipher)}{SM4}
\item \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serpent_(cipher)}{Serpent}, Tnepres
\item \href{https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiny_Encryption_Algorithm}{Tea}, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XTEA}{XTea}
\item and my own simplest symmetric block cipher alogrithms: ZenMatrix, ZenMatrix2
\end{itemize}


\subsection{ZenMatrix a simplest possible algortihm to basically understand symmetric blockcipher}

Starting from a no permutating 1-matrix, where projection is same as base,
ZenMatrix generates a permutating mapping with blocksize 16
a matrix with only one 1 per row and column (rest is 0)
to change position inside block and value offset.

\url{https://area23.at/net/Crypt/ZenMatrixVisualize.aspx}

\begin{figure}
\includegraphics[width=1\textwidth,natwidth=1302,natheight=1002]{2026-01-25_ZenMatrixVisualize.png}
